You can add a comma-separated ROLES or TARGETS column to the manifest and filter against the calling script name or machine role at runtime.
In Wintersys ADT, provisioning scripts are separated by server type (e.g., BuildWebserver.sh, BuildDatabase.sh, BuildAutoscaler.sh, or InitialiseNewServer.sh). By adding a target filter field to software-cache.dat, a single manifest file can govern the entire fleet while each script only installs what it needs.

1. Updated Manifest Format (software-cache.dat)

Add a 6th pipe-delimited field (TARGETS) at the end of each line. Use all for shared base tools, or a comma-separated list of script names / machine roles (e.g., webserver,autoscaler or BuildWebserver.sh).
Schema:
text
NAME:MODE:VERSION|TARGET|EXTRA|INSTALL_DIR|SHA256|TARGETS
Use code with caution.

Example software-cache.dat

ini
# ==============================================================================
# Wintersys ADT Pull-Through S3 Cache Manifest (Target-Filtered)
# Format: NAME:MODE:VERSION|TARGET|EXTRA|INSTALL_DIR|SHA256|TARGETS
# TARGETS: 'all' or comma-separated roles/filenames (e.g., webserver,autoscaler)
# ==============================================================================

# --- Installed on ALL servers ---
s5cmd:binary:2.2.2|https://github.com||/usr/local/bin||all
base-tools:package:1.0|jq curl unzip|hold-pinned|||all

# --- Installed ONLY by Webserver & Autoscaler scripts ---
nginx:source:1.26.2|https://nginx.org|@/webserver/build-nginx-custom.sh --with-threads|||webserver,autoscaler
php8.3-stack:package:8.3|php8.3-fpm php8.3-cli php8.3-mysql php8.3-curl php8.3-zip|@/webserver/setup-php-repo.sh|||webserver,autoscaler

# --- Installed ONLY by Database scripts ---
mariadb-tools:package:10.11|mariadb-backup pv||||database
