3. Usage Inside Specific ADT Scripts

You can filter either by the script's own filename or by a logical role:
• Filter by calling file ($0):
Inside BuildWebserver.sh (if manifest TARGETS lists BuildWebserver.sh or BuildWebserver):sh
"${HOME}/providerscripts/utilities/ApplySoftwareCacheManifest.sh" \
    "${HOME}/runtime/software-cache.dat" "$(/usr/bin/basename "$0")"
Use code with caution.
• Filter by role name:
Inside BuildWebserver.sh or BuildAutoscaler.sh:sh
"${HOME}/providerscripts/utilities/ApplySoftwareCacheManifest.sh" \
    "${HOME}/runtime/software-cache.dat" "webserver"
Use code with caution.
• Filter by a single package name (optional CLI override):
If you ever need a specific script to install just one specific entry from the manifest, you can pass the package name if you add [ "${name}" = "${norm_filter}" ] inside matches_filter().
